# Exact Replit Patch — Source-to-Topic Memory, Author Validation, and Privacy-Safe Partnership Accountability

**Scope:** This patch extends the Library source-memory system and creates an aggregate business impact/outreach candidate program. It does not change login, map rendering, business claim authorization, community feedback, Kinfolk private history, or current launch limits.

**Founder rules encoded below:**

1. A source that answers a Library/Kinfolk question can be remembered for similar future questions only after source validation and topic relevance review.
2. Author/outlet identity is never guessed from a name, photo, domain, geography, or writing style.
3. Members may recommend safe non-minority-owned hotels, museums, and spaces; these spaces can receive only privacy-safe aggregate impact information under an approved partner/outreach policy.
4. Minority-owned businesses may receive a distinct, opt-in **free claim/partnership preview** after human approval. They are never auto-claimed.
5. No business receives an automated email, DM, notification, contact-form message, or partner offer in this release. The code creates an approved, reviewable outreach candidate only. Sending requires a later founder-approved release.
6. No report includes member identities, raw searches, sensitive queries, exact travel plans, follower data, individual visits, or unverified booking claims.

