## Part E — Differentiated partnership behavior

### 1. Non-minority-owned safe spaces (hotel, museum, general venue)

A member can recommend a safe, welcoming non-minority-owned space. It remains discoverable based on real community feedback and safety information. It is **not** pushed to claim, join, ownership programs, ambassador matching, or paid promotion.

The only eligible output is an admin-approved **Safe Space Accountability Brief**, built from thresholded aggregates and explicitly described as community impact—not as a marketing lead. It has no automatic send in this release. If founder later enables contact, the brief must be manually approved and use a public business contact/opt-in basis. It must not disclose exact travel dates, names, demographics, search phrases, bookings, or personal safety/identity data.

### 2. Minority-owned business

Use `black_owned=true` or a designation that is **verified self-designation / owner self-designation**. Do not infer ownership from a business name, neighborhood, product, owner photo, or source outlet.

When the threshold is met, create `minority_owned_claim_preview` or `minority_owned_partnership_preview` in `admin_review`. The approved preview may contain:

```text
Mapping With Melanin community activity, [window]:
• About 35 members saved your business.
• About 55 members opened your official website.
• A public, non-sensitive demand trend: “fruit pebble waffles” appeared in about 85 local discovery searches.

Your listing remains community-added and unclaimed. Claiming is free and lets you manage your public business details. If you choose to learn more, MWM can show optional partnership resources such as menu brainstorming, content guidance, and cultural ambassador opportunities. No member identities or private searches are shared.
```

**No message is automatically sent.** Before an outreach-send release exists, Replit stores the candidate preview for founder/admin review only. When a later approved send route is built, it must link to the secure free claim flow; it may not auto-link an owner, auto-designate ownership, or imply a paid obligation.

### 3. Claim flow

A minority-owned business owner who follows the secure claim route enters the existing pending claim/approval system. Only after approval may they see their own thresholded aggregate dashboard. They never gain access to individual events, raw query history, community feedback authors, private media, claims, or non-public data.

