## Part F — API and authorization

**New member-only outbound route:**

```ts
router.post('/businesses/:businessId/open-official-site', requireAuth, async (req, res) => {
  const business = await loadLiveBusiness(req.params.businessId);
  if (!business?.website) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'OFFICIAL_SITE_UNAVAILABLE' });
  await recordImpact({
    businessId: business.id, userId: req.user.id, eventType: 'official_website_opened',
    surface: 'business_page', isLoadTest: Boolean(req.user.isLoadTest),
  });
  res.json({ destinationUrl: business.website });
});
```

**New owner/admin aggregate route:**

```ts
router.get('/businesses/:businessId/impact-summary', requireAuth, requireBusinessOwnerOrAdmin, async (req, res) => {
  // Verify approved owner link for this business; never use submitted_by_id.
  const rows = await loadVisibleDelayedRollups(req.params.businessId);
  res.json({ period: 'last_7_days', metrics: rows.map(toSafeMetricCopy) });
});
```

`toSafeMetricCopy` returns only metric label, rounded displayed count, window, and safe demand label. It must never return `true_distinct_count`, raw event row, fingerprint, user ID, user city, source surface, age, source query, or time of interaction.

**Admin-only:** `GET /api/admin/business-partnership-candidates`, approve/reject candidate, and any future send action require `requireAdmin`, not merely `requireAuth`.

