## Part G — Mandatory tests and independent proof

1. A Library source with no author metadata is valid when source/policy relevance is sufficient; no demographic field is generated.
2. A self-described Venezuelan outlet is shown with its evidence URL; its identity is not guessed from its name/domain.
3. A Black doctor’s directly relevant published maternal-health research ranks by topic/evidence; an unrelated doctor’s astrophysics article does not rank for maternal health.
4. A source with `held`/404 status never appears as a clickable Library card.
5. Load-test accounts produce no impact events, partnership candidates, source signals, notifications, or outreach.
6. Nine distinct saves produce no visible metric; ten distinct members after 24 hours produce a rounded display metric.
7. A website-open event shows **opened official website**, never booked/visited.
8. A sensitive query cannot create a `demand_signal`.
9. `fruit_pebble_waffles` requires public classification and threshold before a candidate preview contains it.
10. Non-minority safe space creates no claim/join/ambassador invitation; it may only create an admin-approved accountability brief.
11. Minority-owned candidate is created only from verified/self designation and never auto-claimed.
12. Owner impact endpoint rejects an ordinary member with 403 and returns no raw data to a claimed owner.
13. Admin candidate routes return 403 to non-admin users.
14. No outbound business contact is sent in this release; candidates remain `approved_no_send`.
15. Existing community feedback, safety data, claims, and library links continue to pass their current test suites.
